WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.720
If you know that something has to

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.600
change, but you don't know where to

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.880
start and you're already exhausted just

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.920
thinking about what's about to come this

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.680
year because you're so overwhelmed, I

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.920
made this video exactly for you. If we

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.480
start somewhere, we can start right

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.640
here. I'm about to give you some very

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.200
specific and actionable ways to get your

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.200
life together or at the very least, you

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.240
will improve in some way. There's no

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.760
risk or no stakes involved. It's not

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.680
like, oh, you should drink more water

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.560
either, even though you should, but 28

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.680
strategic ways that you can start today

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.800
or this month and eventually have it all

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.960
compound into a completely

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.240
unrecognizable life by December. Every

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.000
single one of them is something that

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.800
I've either done myself or have seen

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.240
help someone a lot within my community

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.040
and I'm not going to waste your time or

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.520
going down this list quickly today. So,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.920
take note of whatever resonates with you

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.480
and leave whatever doesn't. So, if

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.280
you're new here, my name is May. My

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.760
channel's all about improving ourselves,

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.080
whether that's our minds, bodies, and

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.240
spirits. We're going beyond superficial

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.520
and actually changing our schematics,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.960
becoming the person whose life is

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.560
together because of who they are and not

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.680
stuff that they force themselves to do.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.920
Because if you have to force yourself,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.240
that's not really you. But if this

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.280
resonates with you, come and join our

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.040
family. My community is called Stoic

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.720
Angels. We're all here to build. We're

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.640
tight. I even have a group trip to the

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.760
Greek Islands with the community coming

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.200
up this July. And that's how tight we

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.400
are. And you can check my website for

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.080
more details. And then as always, my

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.680
videos have chapters on them because I

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.480
have so many rapid fire points in this

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.400
video. I'm going to be separating them

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.280
into different categories. Now, okay,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.280
let's get into it.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.160
I love this exercise of writing a

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.880
one-pager called who I am in 12 months

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.720
document. I do this at the start of

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.320
every year. We're not even setting goals

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.400
right now. We're just simply thinking of

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.280
anything, even stuff that you think is

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.520
impossible for you at the moment. I've

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.720
had things written down that I didn't

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.080
even believe in the beginning, but

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.440
somehow achieved it by the end of the

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.440
year. But we're not focusing on wishful

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.880
thinking either. So, basically what this

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.800
looks like is I would like you to write

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.840
a description of your future self

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.360
written in the present tense. What do

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.000
they do in their day-to-day life? How do

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:02.200
they handle stress? What does their

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
average weekend or Tuesday look like?

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.120
This will become your compass for every

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.080
decision this year. Even if you forget

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.520
about this one-pager document, it's

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.560
still running in the back of your

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.400
subconscious and you can quietly

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.120
influence the things that you want to do

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.640
in a good way. So, it's excellent for

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.520
setting out intentions for the start of

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.480
the year or even any time that you want

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.240
to start over. And then number two, make

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.280
a list of 10 things that you know you

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.120
need to stop doing. You already know.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.440
Things like pressing the snooze button

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.000
10 times, scrolling on the shopping app

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.760
at 3:00 a.m. in the morning, or even

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.520
some useless situationship that you keep

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.960
thinking about. Write them all down

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.880
because seeing them on paper makes it

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.280
more real to you and you can't change

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.840
the things that you're not aware of. And

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.160
then number three, define five

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.120
non-negotiables. These are your personal

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.600
rules, stuff that you will never budge

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.640
on, things that you do regardless of how

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.360
you feel, what's going on in your life,

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.440
or how tired you are. Mine is actually

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.960
coffee in the morning because I

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.120
genuinely cannot function without it. I

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:59.120
mean, I can, but it's harder. I also

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.560
never speak badly about myself even as a

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.240
joke because I am not a joke. So, think

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.440
about what some of yours can be. This is

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.240
also a great way to set some boundaries.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.720
Another one that I like is I never want

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:11.080
to be shortchanged for anything. So, if

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.880
someone's trying to scam you, you got to

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.560
go after them. Number four, choose one

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.760
therapist, coach, or a book and then

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.400
commit to eight weeks of real work. It's

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.960
always helpful to have someone or

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.560
something to guide you along your

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.880
journey instead of constantly mindlessly

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.160
consuming content like it's

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.680
entertainment. I would pick one resource

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.680
like either getting a therapist or a

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.040
coach or a book that I really love and

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.200
just really go deep into it and actually

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.920
work on those exercises and apply what

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.800
you've learned. Even just a few weeks of

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.920
focusing on something beats a years of

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.680
start and stop, on and off, half-assed

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.920
commitment. Like go all in or do nothing

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.400
at all. And then number five, read more

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.080
books. Someone asked me recently on my

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.400
Instagram stories actually like what

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.920
kind of books do I like? Do I like

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.560
fiction? I personally don't read a lot

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.200
of fiction. I do sometimes, but I'm

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.840
obviously all about self-help,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.720
non-fiction, psychology. So, a few books

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.920
that I like a lot I'm always referencing

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.960
is Atomic Habits by James Clear, which

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.840
is all about micro habits. And also this

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.320
other book called Psycho-Cybernetics and

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.000
this book changed how I understand

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.040
self-image and identity. This was

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.880
written more than half a century ago,

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.440
but it's still more relevant than most

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.920
modern-day self-help books. Your

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.320
self-image truly becomes your entire

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.560
life and it is also the ceiling and

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.760
limitations of how much you can actually

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.480
achieve in your lifetime. So, this book

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.800
teaches you how to rebuild that. If

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.280
you're interested in those, I'll also

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.280
drop the links in the description.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:35.000
Number six, change your passwords and

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.360
enable 2FA on everything. Especially if

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.480
you haven't done this already, get a

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:41.480
strong password with caps and symbols

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.520
and all of it and enable two-factor

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.360
authorization on as many platforms as

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.480
possible. This maybe takes only a few

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.720
hours max, but protects everything that

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.720
you own that lives online. Your digital

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.680
security is a part of having your life

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.960
together. And all you have to do is do

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.040
it once and do it properly because I

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.560
have seen people getting hacked or

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.520
getting scammed and then giving away

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:03.920
their information and that can truly,

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.600
genuinely ruin people's lives. So, even

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:08.400
just spending an hour on this will save

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.280
you so much unnecessary heartache.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.120
Number seven, back up your phone and I

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.600
can't even stress this enough. Most of

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.240
us have our entire lives on our phone,

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.480
photos, contacts, notes, everything. So,

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.080
if your phone died tomorrow, what are

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.840
you going to lose? I've actually had

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.600
this happen to my laptop last year where

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.880
it completely died in the middle of

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.320
editing a video that I spent three days

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.600
on. And because I didn't have a backup

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:31.080
of it, I had to redo everything. And

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.040
then a couple of years ago, my husband

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.440
and I were sitting on our boat and I

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.120
accidentally did this and my husband's

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.520
phone flung into the river and he had

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:42.600
all these photos that were on his phone.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.920
He did not back it up, including photos

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.240
of us, his family, everything. And that

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:49.440
was really tragic. I've also lost my

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.440
phone before with no backup. So, I've

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.280
lost like all of the photos I've had

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.840
from when I was 17 to 20. That's three

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.640
years of my memories that I can't even

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.120
remember and it's so sad because

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.560
everything is so digitized these days.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.840
It's not like I have a physical photo

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.080
album or anything like that. So, it

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.560
takes nothing for you to just set up

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.520
automatic cloud backup today and if not,

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.240
just remember to upload all of your data

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.000
onto a hard drive or somewhere where

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.280
it's safe. I actually recommend doing

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.560
two backups in case something happens to

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.000
the other one because it's not fun to

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.080
lose your memories or your data or

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.160
something that you worked really hard

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.800
on. Number eight, delete the addictive

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.160
apps that you keep checking without even

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.800
thinking about it. You know how there

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.680
are certain apps that will slowly,

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.640
low-key ruin your life over time. For

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:32.520
me, that's extremely addictive games,

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.280
social media that I don't even post on,

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.240
or even shopping apps I keep spending

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.320
money on. Try deleting them for a week,

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.080
literally seven days, and just notice

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.840
how much mental headspace you actually

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.400
get back. And if you miss that app, you

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:45.400
can just download it again. It's not

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:48.080
even a big deal. Number nine, make your

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.960
home screen boring. No social media apps

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.440
on page one. So, what I like to keep on

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.680
there is very productive stuff,

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:55.320
calendar, notes, camera, Google Maps,

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.160
and make the super entertaining and

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:59.560
addictive stuff something that you have

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:01.280
to intentionally seek out and not

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.640
constantly popping out to you. Number

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.240
10, do one week without Reels or TikTok.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:07.480
You don't have to do a total social

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.680
media detox forever. Just try balancing

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.400
it out with seven days to start, maybe

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.360
every now and then, and that's it.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:15.960
Notice what happens to your attention

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.720
span, your sleep, your dopamine levels.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:20.760
Like for example, your ability to be

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.360
bored. Sometimes boring is so good and I

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.800
find that scrolling short-form videos

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:27.120
especially for hours can actually add to

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.840
my stress levels and a high cortisol is

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.360
never a good thing for your health,

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.240
which is why I like YouTube so much

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.040
actually because it's long-form. It's

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.840
slower pace. That way you're not

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:37.200
constantly getting overstimulated all

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.600
the time and you're not constantly

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.600
getting affected by other people's

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.120
opinions a thousand times over because

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.600
they're not even your opinion. So, who

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.240
cares? Try and actually form your own

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:48.040
opinions, right? Like even though I

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.000
myself work in the social media space,

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:52.600
sometimes I'm not even posting because I

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:55.000
genuinely forget to even check Instagram

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:56.845
and stuff. So, it's always good to take

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.320
a bit of breaks here and there. And

00:07:56.845 --> 00:08:00.640
[clears throat] then number 11, master

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.920
an organization tool of choice. I like

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:05.360
to tell people that I myself am also

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.560
neurodivergent and I have ADHD. Not

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.600
because I'm justifying my own

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.760
limitations, but because I can show them

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.760
that despite

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:16.120
having these things affecting my brain,

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.560
I can still be hyper-organized and super

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.120
functional. And I say this because I

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:21.000
always see people being like, oh, this

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.640
is for neurotypical people. Like, I'm

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.960
special. Like, bro, no, you're not. I

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.400
have it, too. A lot of people have it.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:28.680
So, to me, having things like a second

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.600
brain is just not optional. So, pick a

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.800
system, whatever you want to use and

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:34.360
then learn it properly. Like for

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:36.000
example, I like Notion, I like X Tiles,

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.919
ClickUp. And right now, I'm also

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.560
mastering Zapier because it connects to

00:08:37.919 --> 00:08:41.599
everything. It's so incredible. Your

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:44.200
future self or your current self even

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:45.880
needs a place to store all this data and

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.040
things and memories that you're trying

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:49.880
to remember. And your brain just simply

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.320
cannot remember everything. I don't care

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.480
who you are. You just can't. So,

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:56.400
whatever is easy for you, do it. Even if

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.800
it's a notebook. I love the practice

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:59.680
notebook that I designed for my merch

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:02.160
store. I'm always jotting things down in

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.840
there because of the dotted grid. Dotted

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.240
grid. My ADHD brain cannot keep up with

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:08.240
lined notebooks because that doesn't

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.680
work for me, but this works really well

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:11.360
for me. And it helps me learn what kind

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.360
of systems I prefer to work with because

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.760
I'm always changing things and sometimes

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.000
I have favorites. I also have

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.840
affirmations in the back, which are

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.200
great reminders. Anyways, I designed

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.120
this myself. It's in my merch Number 12,

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.680
track every dollar for 30 days. You

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.120
don't even have to do this forever, but

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.760
just enough to know where your money is

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.400
going. Every coffee that you're buying

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.280
at Starbucks, every subscription you

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:32.040
have, every single time that you're

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:33.600
treating yourself. We're not judging it,

