right now, but there's a lot of other

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:22.040
things that you can do. A lot of people

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:24.000
do cut their hair or get a new hair

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.360
color or even shave their head bald or

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.159
their eyebrows. And they do this

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:28.640
whenever they want to start over or

00:19:27.159 --> 00:19:32.320
after a breakup and they want to start a

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.320
new chapter because it works.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.400
Number 24, reconnect with five people

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.760
that you miss but never message. I think

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:41.320
a lot of us are so disconnected from one

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:42.800
another more than ever before and just

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.919
looking at someone's Instagram stories

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:46.120
doesn't mean that you're staying in

00:19:43.919 --> 00:19:48.000
touch with them. So send them a message,

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:50.400
respond to their social media posts,

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.080
call them, send them a text. The

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.360
awkwardness of you feeling like you have

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:55.600
to reach out and then reaching out only

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:57.400
last about 30 seconds, but the regret of

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:59.680
losing that connection will last for as

00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:01.840
long as you lose that connection. I'm

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.760
very sure that most of the time people

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.640
will appreciate this, especially if

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.240
they're a friend, unless I don't know if

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.800
it's like an ex or a complicated

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:10.760
situation, then obviously that's

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.800
different. But for the most part, if

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:14.040
it's like an old classmate or neighbor,

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:16.440
I'm pretty sure that they're going to

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:19.080
appreciate your gesture. Number 25,

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:21.160
learn how to say no cleanly. A lot of

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:23.040
people don't even know how to say no, so

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:25.120
they don't get what they want. So,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.400
practice saying this, I'm sure that

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:28.000
there are things that you don't like.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:30.000
So, whenever that comes up, you can just

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.280
say it with grace, like, "Oh, this is

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.920
not for me, but thank you." And practice

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:36.440
until it feels natural to you. Do not

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:38.360
explain yourself. Do not apologize for

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:40.720
not liking something. If there's someone

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:42.560
in your life who is very draining and

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:44.600
you have to see them and you can't get

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:47.080
away from them, name what you need from

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:48.400
them and state it clearly, especially if

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.200
you can't avoid them forever. Like, if

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:52.840
they're a family member or a classmate

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:54.320
or a boss. However, they react to you is

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:56.040
not your responsibility, but the things

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:58.360
that you communicate and the peace that

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:59.680
you get from it is your responsibility.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.760
So, focus on the things that you can

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:03.520
control. Just keep things simple and

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:06.480
every no to something wrong is a yes to

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:08.600
something right.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.960
Number 26, do something you're slightly

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.240
scared of once a month. Do not confront

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.600
your greatest fear just yet, that's a

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:16.120
huge step, but something that you're

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:18.040
even just slightly afraid of, even if

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:20.000
it's kind of silly and dumb, like asking

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.600
for more sauce at a restaurant or

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.080
confronting a difficult conversation,

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:24.240
which is actually very useful. Because

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.680
if you don't do that, it will keep

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:27.520
haunting you, right? So, putting

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:29.240
yourself out there, sharing your art or

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:31.520
your music with other people, like

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:33.000
having courage is a skill and a muscle,

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:35.320
and the more you do this, the easier it

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:37.320
gets. And then the more desensitized you

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:39.440
are to that fear. Like, for example, one

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:41.040
fear that I have is jumping into the

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.720
water, even if there's nothing in front

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.920
of me and it still took me a while to

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:46.320
jump. Eventually, I still got over it

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:48.360
and I jumped. And this happened to me

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:50.400
when I was in Tulum, Mexico, and I was

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:52.440
just swimming in this gorgeous natural

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:54.240
pool, and everyone was jumping.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:56.360
Eventually, I jumped. Even though I

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:58.000
technically body slammed the water, it

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:59.480
wasn't very graceful, but at least I did

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.000
it and I'm able to practice more of

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:02.360
that. The more I do it, the easier it

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.880
will get. I'm not going to lie, my

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:05.679
nerves never went away. I did it so

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:07.360
scared, but at least I know that I've

00:22:05.679 --> 00:22:09.880
done this before and I didn't end up

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:12.280
alive, and even toddlers can do this, so

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:14.440
I can do this, too. Number 27, start

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:15.960
junk journaling instead of junk food,

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:17.720
junk journaling. This is a great

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:20.160
journaling prompt that I have where it's

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:22.440
not even a prompt. No structure,

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:23.920
nothing, just dump whatever goes on in

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:26.320
your head onto paper so that you can

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:28.120
practice and process the stuff that's

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:29.880
too difficult for you to figure out in

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:31.840
your head. Even if it's just a few

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:35.000
minutes of messy thinking going onto

00:22:31.840 --> 00:22:37.440
paper will prevent hours of mess in your

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:39.880
life. And then you can actually learn to

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:41.760
dissect whatever is going on and make

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.400
sense of whatever feels messy to you.

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:47.320
Number 28, take 10 photos of yourself

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:49.360
that you genuinely love. This is a great

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:51.200
exercise to gain more confidence. You're

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:52.520
taking photos not for anyone else, but

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:54.280
for yourself, and this is how you can

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.640
learn your angles. You can understand

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:57.520
what kind of lighting looks good on you

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:59.280
and you can practice until you can

00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:01.160
capture images of yourself that makes

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:02.520
you think, "That's really me. That's

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:04.960
what I look like." And this is

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.320
especially useful if you're afraid of

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:08.720
the way that you look. So, if you can

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:10.640
have all this visual evidence that you

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:12.640
can and you do look good in a certain

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:14.400
way and you like how you look and you

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:15.960
know that these are your angles and you

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:18.679
can replicate them, then you'll be able

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:20.360
to have a better relationship with your

00:23:18.679 --> 00:23:22.800
appearance, your style, and your

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:25.080
relationship with your own image matters

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:27.040
so much more than you think. It affects

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:28.920
everything else going on in your life,

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:31.200
and this can be as simple with starting

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:33.360
with just liking 10 photos of yourself.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:35.000
And if you still don't feel good, go to

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:36.600
point number four and you can hash it

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:38.000
out with a therapist or journal it out

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:39.840
and figure out why that is.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:41.840
Self-awareness is everything. Again,

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:43.280
like I said, you don't have to do all of

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:45.080
these things. You don't even have to do

00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:46.960
them in order, but just pick a few of

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:48.320
them, maybe three, especially the ones

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:50.160
that you feel like you need, but you're

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.720
a bit scared of them, but then you also

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:53.320
know that they will actually change the

00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:54.920
way that you see yourself and your life.

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.360
And then tell me what you want to work

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:58.160
on in the comments, because writing it

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:59.920
down makes it feel even more real. You

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:01.280
can even leave a comment just so that

00:23:59.920 --> 00:24:02.600
you can keep track of what you're

00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:04.560
working on so that you can come back

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:06.120
later on and you'll see that comment and

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:08.080
you'll be able to have proof of the

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:09.880
exact moment that you decide to actually

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:11.600
do something different about it, and

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:13.560
that's yet another way to show up for

00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:15.360
yourself. This is what I'm about. This

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:17.720
is what my Stoic Angels community is

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:21.200
about, and I believe in you, angels. I

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:21.200
will see you in the next video.

